                <pb facs="0321" n="245" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg245"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">651.116 Nitrate/81: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Straus</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-02-18T18:00:00-05:00">February 18, 1935—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>60. <hi rendition="#italic">New York Times</hi> publishes Paris despatch that
                    United States has been shut out of French nitrate market this year, Chile and
                    Norway receiving 80,000 and 20,000 tons respectively. If appropriate at this
                    stage, please take matter up with French again, emphasizing this Government’s
                    position as outlined in Department’s 469, November 21, 1934.<anchor n="40"
                        xml:id="d196-f1"/> Please advise Department by cable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
